course: dictionary
lesson: 6484
title: Words that name a job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A navigator is a person who works out the way to go and tells the driver or pilot where to turn. The word comes from «navigate», which means to find your way. «Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific in double canoes, finding their way by the stars, waves and birds.» Here the navigators were the people who worked out the route.
explain: The clues around a word tell you its meaning. «Tupaia, a navigator from Tahiti, sailed with Cook, helped guide the ship and helped him talk with the Māori.» Guiding the ship is a clue: a navigator helps guide the ship, so the word names a job that finds the way.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning. A navigator can also be a sat-nav or app that shows the way, or a sailor-explorer in history. Read the sentence to choose the right meaning. On a trip, the person with the map is the navigator, and a sat-nav can be a navigator too.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Put «a person who works out the route» in place of navigators in «Polynesian navigators sailed double canoes across the Pacific». If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A navigator works out the route and tells the driver or pilot where to go.
fact: In history, a navigator was a sailor-explorer who found new sea routes.
fact: Polynesian navigators read the stars, waves, winds and birds to find their way across the Pacific.
fact: A sat-nav or app can also be called a navigator, because it shows the way.
fact: Useful phrases are «act as navigator» and «a great navigator».
exercise: «Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific in double canoes.» What does navigators mean here? | *People who worked out the way across the sea | Birds that fly very far | Boats made from wood and metal | People who sell fish at the market
exercise: On a car trip, who is the navigator? | The person who fills the petrol tank | The person who drives the car | *The person with the map who tells the driver where to turn | The person who sleeps in the back
exercise: Which tools did Polynesian navigators use to find their way? | Clocks and calculators | *Stars, waves and birds | Street lamps and road signs | Telephones and radios
test: «Tupaia, a navigator from Tahiti, sailed with Cook and helped guide the ship.» What was Tupaia's job on the ship? | A captain who gave the orders | *A navigator who helped guide the ship | A passenger with no job to do | A cook who made the meals
test: Jayden reads «a great navigator» in a history book. What does navigator most likely mean here? | A brand of map | *A skilled sailor-explorer who found the way | A sat-nav in a car | A sleepy passenger
exam: On a car trip, the navigator reads the map and does what? | Drives the car as fast as possible | *Tells the driver where to go | Pays for the petrol | Sleeps until they arrive
